NOT THE TEST SET. Superseded per R-172.

This file was built over [era_floor, topup_end] -- which swept all 471
consumed-fragment windows into what was meant to be the held-out test set --
and was then FILTERED IN PLACE by BE to slugs > 1787650200 (337 windows).

BE overwrote the rejected 808-window content when filtering, so the artifact
R-172(3) asks to preserve no longer exists. That was BE's error: a rejected
artifact is evidence. This file is the post-filter state, kept as the closest
available provenance, and is NOT to be used as the Phase-2 test surface.

The clean rebuild, with BOTH population bounds resolved as one interval, is
harmful_exposure_rows_v3_topup.json.
